WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:07.600
Mō tātou, a, mō ka uri a muri ake nei

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:16.470
We’re currently working on the sport and
recreation plans for the Kaiapoi East Regeneration

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:19.840
Area and have been meeting with the sports
clubs that are going to be located here.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:23.640
During this design phase, we’re looking
at the positioning for the sports fields,

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:26.920
car parking, club room facility, public toilets

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.480
and also spaces for the bmx track and dog park.

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:38.960
The Kaiapoi Food Forest was a popular request
during the development of the Recovery Plan.

00:00:38.969 --> 00:00:44.050
In September, a number of mature fruit trees
from empty sections in the Regeneration areas

00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:46.360
were relocated to the food forest site.

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:49.560
And then the community-led project really
got off the ground with the opening

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:51.200
and community planting day.

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:58.429
It was the number one request on all the community
consultation and it's just great to see something

00:00:58.429 --> 00:01:00.690
visible and above ground happening.

00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:05.790
It's always more exciting to plant trees than
put sewer lines underground and the community

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:08.080
have turned out in force and it's all go.

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:12.910
Many of the trees planted were donated from
groups and tree-nurseries located from all

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:14.400
across Canterbury.

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:17.640
Organisers were stunned by the support shown
by the community.

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:21.440
We've had amazing support for the Kaiapoi
Food Forest.

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:26.110
So many groups have come down, so Kaiapoi
Garden Club, we've got Cactus - the leadership

00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:27.600
programme from Kaiapoi High.

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:30.440
We've got the Mayor, we've got councillors,
we've got,

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:33.360
what, probably 150 odd people 
down here I'd imagine Lesley?

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:35.400
Dude, I'm running out of fingers to count.

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:39.760
Although a large amount of work has been done,
it will take years

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:41.960
for the project come to full fruition.

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:46.090
The Food Forest is being planted in a layered
system with larger fruit trees sheltering

00:01:46.090 --> 00:01:48.240
smaller bushes and plants.

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:51.830
It's quite a lot of intensive work initially,
for the first couple of years.

00:01:51.830 --> 00:01:56.530
So you set that major fruit tree, or nut tree
and then underneath that you put a smaller

00:01:56.530 --> 00:01:59.570
fruit tree and underneath that you put raspberries
or berries.

00:01:59.570 --> 00:02:04.000
Then underneath that, root crop and ground
cover, so you've got five layers over the

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:05.400
top of each other.

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:12.951
And the food forest, isn’t just about providing
food, it’s also an opportunity for the community

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:14.620
to connect with one another.

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:16.840
I think this is something that's lacking.

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:21.330
It's people getting out and working with each
other and spending time with each other.

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:26.000
So for me, it's not necessarily so much about
a food forest, it's about everything else

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:27.720
that goes with it.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:34.200
It's incredibly humbling and what an amazing
community to be part of.

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:35.640
Thanks everyone.

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:41.080
The Food Forest will really be coming into
its own about March next year, and the public

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:42.960
will be able to come down and enjoy it.

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:47.349
We'll be installing a new pedestrian gate
next to the existing gate on Cass Street.

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:53.600
In the next update we’ll meet Gavin Lake,
the Council’s Roading Recovery Programme Manager

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:58.310
He’s supervising two roading projects that
kick off in January - The new road link in

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:02.960
Kaiapoi East and in Kaiapoi South, the repair
of Courtenay Drive, and parts of

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:06.360
Charters Street and Wyber Place.

